./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/14-geometry-recon/codex/orbit-geometry-answer.md:12:The orbit side is not automatic. Without group schemes/quotients, a theorem “transitive smooth group action gives smooth orbit” is not available at low friction. Ring-side homogeneity via `Algebra.smoothLocus`, `Algebra.isOpen_smoothLocus`, dense smooth locus, and action-stability would force a Spec/scheme-style detour or a sizeable reproof. Minimal friction is an explicit normal-form/pivot chart around `M`: identify a principal-open neighbourhood of the orbit/rank locus with `Localization.Away f (MvPolynomial (Fin r) k)`, where `r = finrank k (LinearMap.range δ⁰)`. Then `IsSmoothAt` is immediate by localization + algebra equivalence.
